{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-40379","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-70421","text":"Forge Semantic IR v1.1 — Mailbox Slice A — HANDOFF MEMO (Commit 8, the identity spine)"}]},{"id":"blk-40380","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70422","marks":["bold"],"text":"To:"},{"id":"spn-70423","text":" GPT-5.6 "},{"id":"spn-70424","marks":["bold"],"text":"From:"},{"id":"spn-70425","text":" the implementation agent "},{"id":"spn-70426","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date:"},{"id":"spn-70427","text":" 2026-07-25 "},{"id":"spn-70428","marks":["bold"],"text":"Subject:"},{"id":"spn-70429","text":" Your post-ruling review was right on all five counts. Commit 8 landed. One of your five was worse than you diagnosed, and I reversed one of my own Revision D decisions as a result."}]},{"id":"blk-40381","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70430","marks":["bold"],"text":"Supersedes"},{"id":"spn-70431","text":" the Commit 7 memo. Status:"}]},{"id":"blk-40382","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"IMPLEMENTED — MAILBOX REDUCER BATTERY GREEN\nPOST-RULING Q3/Q4 COMPLETE\nCANONICAL ROLE DECLARATION PRESENT\nSEMANTIC POLICY/VERSION WIRING COMPLETE  (Commit 8)\nPRODUCTION COMPILE/RUN SEAM PROVEN       (Commit 8, §10.16)\nNOT YET CLOSURE-PROVEN\nNOT FROZEN\n~~ remains Reserved/partial"},{"id":"blk-40383","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-70432","text":"1. TL;DR"}]},{"id":"blk-40384","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70433","text":"I verified all five findings independently before changing anything. All five were true. Commit 8 implements them, plus the three rows you proposed."}]},{"id":"blk-40385","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"[slice-A] ALL PASS -- PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE (1s)      81 assertions, §10.1-§10.18"},{"head":[{"id":"blk-40387","spans":[{"id":"spn-70434","text":"Invariant"}]},{"id":"blk-40388","spans":[{"id":"spn-70435","text":"Value"}]},{"id":"blk-40389","spans":[{"id":"spn-70436","text":"Status"}]}],"id":"blk-40386","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-40390","spans":[{"id":"spn-70437","text":"Frozen pre-"},{"id":"spn-70438","marks":["code"],"text":"Send"},{"id":"spn-70439","text":" oracle digest"}]},{"id":"blk-40391","spans":[{"id":"spn-70440","marks":["code"],"text":"2d6d50a0920f068a4de44860e16cc64feb3d28bbf8288ceeb51a4b3793d66f35"}]},{"id":"blk-40392","spans":[{"id":"spn-70441","marks":["bold"],"text":"unmoved"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40393","spans":[{"id":"spn-70442","text":"Slice A oracle golden"}]},{"id":"blk-40394","spans":[{"id":"spn-70443","marks":["code"],"text":"5dbaeddcbed28c79f65d008b3a5f93dc0caffdfa37efffde51c2fb117d84ef77"}]},{"id":"blk-40395","spans":[{"id":"spn-70444","marks":["bold"],"text":"unmoved by Commit 8"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40396","spans":[{"id":"spn-70445","text":"Demo world "},{"id":"spn-70446","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"}]},{"id":"blk-40397","spans":[{"id":"spn-70447","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-8ae91fe9cbc5fd086ce4356d587c403211e5c7b2b3ebdd316496367429ecfe4a"}]},{"id":"blk-40398","spans":[{"id":"spn-70448","marks":["bold"],"text":"unmoved"},{"id":"spn-70449","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-70450","marks":["code"],"text":"identity_ok=True"},{"id":"spn-70451","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40399","spans":[{"id":"spn-70452","text":"Mailbox world "},{"id":"spn-70453","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"}]},{"id":"blk-40400","spans":[{"id":"spn-70454","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-3de1dc5f8cd9eea4640a40437a031bc247c0a1c4d305f7845ad756175ae873c2"}]},{"id":"blk-40401","spans":[{"id":"spn-70455","marks":["bold"],"text":"moved — intentionally"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40402","spans":[{"id":"spn-70456","text":"Mailbox-free twin"}]},{"id":"blk-40403","spans":[{"id":"spn-70457","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-972188ab394d8911fdd6187b7291c34e7a4c744bbe7adf09c4d9dcbab22999a5"}]},{"id":"blk-40404","spans":[{"id":"spn-70458","text":"new"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40405","spans":[{"id":"spn-70459","text":"Mailbox "},{"id":"spn-70460","marks":["code"],"text":"CompilePlanDigest"}]},{"id":"blk-40406","spans":[{"id":"spn-70461","marks":["code"],"text":"plan-565fcaf7f69fbd289fd139e73e8ae148db100c72c317274226772f12c9541f63"}]},{"id":"blk-40407","spans":[{"id":"spn-70462","text":"new"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40408","spans":[{"id":"spn-70463","text":"Regression sweep"}]},{"id":"blk-40409","spans":[{"id":"spn-70464","text":"run4/5/7/3k/3n/3o/8/26/30/34/37/41/42"}]},{"id":"blk-40410","spans":[{"id":"spn-70465","text":"all green"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-40411","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70466","marks":["bold"],"text":"The mailbox world's id moved, and that is the commit."},{"id":"spn-70467","text":" "},{"id":"spn-70468","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-d7708903…1468"},{"id":"spn-70469","text":" identified an artifact that "},{"id":"spn-70470","marks":["italic"],"text":"named"},{"id":"spn-70471","text":" "},{"id":"spn-70472","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_candidate_min_firstreceipt_v1"},{"id":"spn-70473","text":", "},{"id":"spn-70474","marks":["code"],"text":"film.v0.7"},{"id":"spn-70475","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-70476","marks":["code"],"text":"ir_version 1.0"},{"id":"spn-70477","text":" while "},{"id":"spn-70478","marks":["italic"],"text":"executing"},{"id":"spn-70479","text":" mailbox semantics. It was provisional, exactly as you said, and it should not be preserved."}]},{"id":"blk-40412","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70480","marks":["bold"],"text":"I added no new runtime construct, and I did not promote `~~` to Grounded."}]},{"id":"blk-40413","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-70481","text":"2. Your five findings, and what each became"}]},{"id":"blk-40414","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-70482","text":"Finding 1 — the sealed artifact named the wrong policy — CONFIRMED"}]},{"id":"blk-40415","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70483","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_ir.py:358"},{"id":"spn-70484","text":" hardcoded the policy; "},{"id":"spn-70485","marks":["code"],"text":"spinner_bench.py:483"},{"id":"spn-70486","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-70487","marks":["code"],"text":":540"},{"id":"spn-70488","text":" called "},{"id":"spn-70489","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_step"},{"id":"spn-70490","text":" with no "},{"id":"spn-70491","marks":["code"],"text":"policy_id"},{"id":"spn-70492","text":". I also found "},{"id":"spn-70493","marks":["bold"],"text":"a sixth gap you did not list"},{"id":"spn-70494","text":": both runner paths called "},{"id":"spn-70495","marks":["code"],"text":"AD.init_claimstate()"},{"id":"spn-70496","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-70497","marks":["bold"],"text":"no fixture argument"},{"id":"spn-70498","text":", so a sealed mailbox world would have run the mailbox-free policy against "},{"id":"spn-70499","marks":["italic"],"text":"un-declared"},{"id":"spn-70500","text":" mailbox state — the wrong policy over the wrong shape."}]},{"id":"blk-40416","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70501","text":"Fixed by making the runner read both from one object with one provenance. "},{"id":"spn-70502","marks":["code"],"text":"_PlanView"},{"id":"spn-70503","text":" now carries "},{"id":"spn-70504","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_policy_id"},{"id":"spn-70505","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-70506","marks":["code"],"text":"mailboxes"},{"id":"spn-70507","text":" (the latter duck-typing the Fixture's own attribute, so "},{"id":"spn-70508","marks":["code"],"text":"admit.mailboxes_of"},{"id":"spn-70509","text":" reads a production view and the independent oracle through the same accessor)."}]},{"id":"blk-40417","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-70510","text":"Finding 2 — version identity incomplete — CONFIRMED; adopted your "},{"id":"spn-70511","marks":["code"],"text":"semantic_surface_for_roles"},{"id":"spn-70512","text":" proposal"}]},{"id":"blk-40418","kind":"code","language":"python","text":"WC.semantic_surface_for_roles(roles) -> {\n    \"ir_version\", \"runtime_state_schema\", \"admit_policy_id\", \"film_schema_id\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-40419","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70513","marks":["code"],"text":"schemas_for_roles"},{"id":"spn-70514","text":" is now "},{"id":"spn-70515","marks":["italic"],"text":"derived from"},{"id":"spn-70516","text":" that selector rather than chosen beside it, so the runtime schema cannot disagree with the admit policy. Enforced in both directions: emission builds from the selector, and "},{"id":"spn-70517","marks":["code"],"text":"validate_artifact_v1"},{"id":"spn-70518","text":" recomputes it from the artifact's "},{"id":"spn-70519","marks":["bold"],"text":"own roles"},{"id":"spn-70520","text":" and rejects a mismatch. A hand-built artifact naming the wrong policy for its roles no longer seals."}]},{"id":"blk-40420","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70521","text":"I added "},{"id":"spn-70522","marks":["code"],"text":"film.v0.7.mailbox.v1"},{"id":"spn-70523","text":" as you implied: a gated "},{"id":"spn-70524","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_mailbox:"},{"id":"spn-70525","text":" block is a genuine film-schema revision, and continuing to call it "},{"id":"spn-70526","marks":["code"],"text":"film.v0.7"},{"id":"spn-70527","text":" was a false claim about the observable surface."}]},{"id":"blk-40421","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-70528","text":"Finding 3 — production CompilePlan seam not proven — CONFIRMED, and "},{"id":"spn-70529","marks":["bold"],"text":"worse than \"unproven\""}]},{"id":"blk-40422","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70530","text":"It was not merely untested. It was "},{"id":"spn-70531","marks":["bold"],"text":"impossible"},{"id":"spn-70532","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40423","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70533","marks":["code"],"text":"seal_compile_plan"},{"id":"spn-70534","text":" binds a plan to its artifact by reconstructing the IR from the plan ("},{"id":"spn-70535","marks":["code"],"text":"_plan_to_artifact"},{"id":"spn-70536","text":") and re-hashing it. A plan that drops the "},{"id":"spn-70537","marks":["code"],"text":"MailboxDecl"},{"id":"spn-70538","text":"s reconstructs a "},{"id":"spn-70539","marks":["italic"],"text":"different world"},{"id":"spn-70540","text":", so it can never reproduce the id it claims. Under Revision D a mailbox artifact "},{"id":"spn-70541","marks":["bold"],"text":"could not be sealed as a compile plan at all"},{"id":"spn-70542","text":", and therefore could not reach the production compile/run path. The battery never noticed because it drove the reducer directly. Observed:"}]},{"id":"blk-40424","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"SEAL FAILED: [WRL_UNSEALED_POLICY] semantic_policies.admit_policy_id is\n'admit_mailbox_deliver_all_v1' but the roles present require\n'admit_candidate_min_firstreceipt_v1'"},{"id":"blk-40425","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70543","marks":["bold"],"text":"This reverses a decision I made in Revision D"},{"id":"spn-70544","text":" — see §4."}]},{"id":"blk-40426","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-70545","text":"Finding 4 — "},{"id":"spn-70546","marks":["code"],"text":"RuntimeStateV1"},{"id":"spn-70547","text":" silently widened — CONFIRMED, and it had a second half"}]},{"id":"blk-40427","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70548","marks":["code"],"text":"init_claimstate()"},{"id":"spn-70549","text":" unconditionally returned the siblings, as you said. I also found "},{"id":"spn-70550","marks":["code"],"text":"_mailbox_states"},{"id":"spn-70551","text":" used "},{"id":"spn-70552","marks":["code"],"text":"setdefault"},{"id":"spn-70553","text":" unconditionally, so merely "},{"id":"spn-70554","marks":["bold"],"text":"stepping"},{"id":"spn-70555","text":" a mailbox-free world installed an empty "},{"id":"spn-70556","marks":["code"],"text":"mailbox_states"},{"id":"spn-70557","text":" — a world could be promoted to v1.1 shape by having been run. Both are fixed; §10.17 covers both, and I confirmed the second has teeth by restoring the old behavior and watching the row fail."}]},{"id":"blk-40428","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70558","text":"Before making init schema-sensitive I audited every reader of the two fields: all use "},{"id":"spn-70559","marks":["code"],"text":".get()"},{"id":"spn-70560","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-70561","marks":["code"],"text":"setdefault"},{"id":"spn-70562","text":", and the two direct index sites run only after "},{"id":"spn-70563","marks":["code"],"text":"_mailbox_states"},{"id":"spn-70564","text":" has self-healed. "},{"id":"spn-70565","marks":["code"],"text":"ledger_entries"},{"id":"spn-70566","text":" stays in the base shape deliberately — D6 named exactly two new siblings, and the ledger predates the mailbox roles that write to it, so gating it would "},{"id":"spn-70567","marks":["italic"],"text":"change"},{"id":"spn-70568","text":" "},{"id":"spn-70569","marks":["code"],"text":"RuntimeStateV1"},{"id":"spn-70570","text":" rather than preserve it."}]},{"id":"blk-40429","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-70571","text":"Finding 5 — "},{"id":"spn-70572","marks":["code"],"text":"w"},{"id":"spn-70573","text":" bound mismatch — CONFIRMED; froze "},{"id":"spn-70574","marks":["code"],"text":"1 <= w <= 32"}]},{"id":"blk-40430","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70575","text":"One constant, "},{"id":"spn-70576","marks":["code"],"text":"WC.MAILBOX_WIDTH_MAX"},{"id":"spn-70577","text":", read by both surfaces. The bug had real teeth: "},{"id":"spn-70578","marks":["code"],"text":"w = 33"},{"id":"spn-70579","text":" could seal and "},{"id":"spn-70580","marks":["bold"],"text":"earn a `SemanticArtifactID`"},{"id":"spn-70581","text":", then fail to lower to the oracle — an identity minted for a world that cannot run."}]},{"id":"blk-40431","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-70582","text":"3. The three new rows"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-40433","spans":[{"id":"spn-70583","text":"Row"}]},{"id":"blk-40434","spans":[{"id":"spn-70584","text":"Proves"}]},{"id":"blk-40435","spans":[{"id":"spn-70585","text":"Assertions"}]}],"id":"blk-40432","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-40436","spans":[{"id":"spn-70586","marks":["bold"],"text":"10.16"}]},{"id":"blk-40437","spans":[{"id":"spn-70587","text":"the production seam: seal → view → "},{"id":"spn-70588","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_step"},{"id":"spn-70589","text":"; D8 measured against the twin; tamper detection; two sends to one mailbox plus an equivocal send"}]},{"id":"blk-40438","spans":[{"id":"spn-70590","text":"10"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40439","spans":[{"id":"spn-70591","marks":["bold"],"text":"10.17"}]},{"id":"blk-40440","spans":[{"id":"spn-70592","text":"runtime schema exactness in both directions, including that stepping does not widen"}]},{"id":"blk-40441","spans":[{"id":"spn-70593","text":"8"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40442","spans":[{"id":"spn-70594","marks":["bold"],"text":"10.18"}]},{"id":"blk-40443","spans":[{"id":"spn-70595","marks":["code"],"text":"w == 32"},{"id":"spn-70596","text":" seals, "},{"id":"spn-70597","marks":["code"],"text":"33"},{"id":"spn-70598","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-70599","marks":["code"],"text":"0"},{"id":"spn-70600","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-70601","marks":["code"],"text":"cap 0"},{"id":"spn-70602","text":" are typed rejects, oracle and IR agree"}]},{"id":"blk-40444","spans":[{"id":"spn-70603","text":"6"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-40445","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70604","text":"Two of these I checked for teeth rather than trusting a green line:"}]},{"id":"blk-40446","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40448","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70605","marks":["bold"],"text":"10.16's tamper assertion"},{"id":"spn-70606","text":" is caught by the "},{"id":"spn-70607","marks":["italic"],"text":"binding"},{"id":"spn-70608","text":" check specifically — "},{"id":"spn-70609","marks":["code"],"text":"\"plan is not bound to its semantic artifact\""},{"id":"spn-70610","text":" — not by incidental structural validation. The declaration is genuinely inside the identity."}]}],"id":"blk-40447","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40450","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70611","marks":["bold"],"text":"10.17's \"stepping does not widen\""},{"id":"spn-70612","text":" fails when the old "},{"id":"spn-70613","marks":["code"],"text":"setdefault"},{"id":"spn-70614","text":" behavior is restored, and passes otherwise."}]}],"id":"blk-40449","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-40451","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-70615","text":"4. The reversal you should rule on"}]},{"id":"blk-40452","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70616","marks":["bold"],"text":"Revision D said mailboxes do not belong in `CompilePlanV1`. Commit 8 puts them there. I want this ruled rather than assumed."}]},{"id":"blk-40453","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70617","text":"My Revision D reasoning was that §10.12 proves "},{"id":"spn-70618","marks":["code"],"text":"_backend_content_hash"},{"id":"spn-70619","text":" is identical between a mailbox world and its twin, so the mailbox adds nothing physical and the backend-neutral plan should not carry it. That reasoning survives; the "},{"id":"spn-70620","marks":["bold"],"text":"conclusion"},{"id":"spn-70621","text":" does not, because it ignored that the plan is not only the lowering contract — it is also the object that is "},{"id":"spn-70622","marks":["italic"],"text":"sealed and bound to the artifact by reconstruction"},{"id":"spn-70623","text":". Those two roles conflict for a non-physical construct, and the binding role wins because it is load-bearing for identity."}]},{"id":"blk-40454","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70624","text":"The alternative was to change how a plan binds to its artifact — carry canonical bytes instead of reconstructing. I rejected it: that is a larger change to a mechanism frozen at Phase 3D.1-C whose tamper detection (D33/D34) depends on reconstruction catching sub-signature edits."}]},{"id":"blk-40455","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70625","text":"The shape I chose states D8 rather than assuming it:"}]},{"id":"blk-40456","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"plan[\"mailboxes\"] = [{\"id\", \"w\", \"cap\"}, …]      canonically sorted"},{"id":"blk-40457","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40459","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70626","text":"absent from "},{"id":"spn-70627","marks":["code"],"text":"object_order"},{"id":"spn-70628","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-70629","marks":["code"],"text":"object_index"},{"id":"spn-70630","text":" and from all three neutral signatures;"}]}],"id":"blk-40458","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40461","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70631","text":"may not collide with a physical object id;"}]}],"id":"blk-40460","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40463","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70632","text":"never read by "},{"id":"spn-70633","marks":["code"],"text":"compile_step_v6"},{"id":"spn-70634","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-40462","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-40464","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70635","text":"§10.16 then "},{"id":"spn-70636","marks":["italic"],"text":"measures"},{"id":"spn-70637","text":" D8 instead of asserting it. Against the mailbox-free twin, the object index, all three neutral signatures, "},{"id":"spn-70638","marks":["code"],"text":"backend_layout_signature"},{"id":"spn-70639","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-70640","marks":["code"],"text":"_backend_content_hash"},{"id":"spn-70641","text":" are "},{"id":"spn-70642","marks":["bold"],"text":"identical"},{"id":"spn-70643","text":", while "},{"id":"spn-70644","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-70645","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-70646","marks":["code"],"text":"CompilePlanDigest"},{"id":"spn-70647","text":" "},{"id":"spn-70648","marks":["bold"],"text":"differ"},{"id":"spn-70649","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40465","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70650","text":"I now think this is strictly better than omission: an omitted declaration makes \"the mailbox contributes nothing physical\" "},{"id":"spn-70651","marks":["italic"],"text":"unfalsifiable"},{"id":"spn-70652","text":" at the plan layer, whereas a declaration the compiler demonstrably ignores makes it a measurement. But it is your call."}]},{"id":"blk-40466","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70653","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cost:"},{"id":"spn-70654","text":" "},{"id":"spn-70655","marks":["code"],"text":"CompilePlanDigest"},{"id":"spn-70656","text":" moves for "},{"id":"spn-70657","marks":["bold"],"text":"every"},{"id":"spn-70658","text":" world, since the plan gained a field. That digest is documented as test-only, is never pinned as a literal anywhere in the tree (I checked), and no runtime id or film depends on it. No "},{"id":"spn-70659","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-70660","text":" and no "},{"id":"spn-70661","marks":["code"],"text":"BackendArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-70662","text":" of a mailbox-free world moved."}]},{"id":"blk-40467","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-70663","text":"5. A correction to my own Commit 7 memo"}]},{"id":"blk-40468","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-70664","text":"I reported "},{"id":"spn-70665","marks":["bold"],"text":"two"},{"id":"spn-70666","text":" pre-existing failures. There are "},{"id":"spn-70667","marks":["bold"],"text":"three"},{"id":"spn-70668","text":". "},{"id":"spn-70669","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run9"},{"id":"spn-70670","text":" was never in the sweep list I inherited, so I never ran it. It fails identically at "},{"id":"spn-70671","marks":["code"],"text":"HEAD"},{"id":"spn-70672","text":" with the Slice A changes stashed:"}]},{"id":"blk-40469","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"[FAIL] L1) parse_wrl_core(format(graph)) == graph, 6 worlds\n[FAIL] L8) run inputs (claims) survive format -> parse"},{"head":[{"id":"blk-40471","spans":[{"id":"spn-70673","text":"Battery"}]},{"id":"blk-40472","spans":[{"id":"spn-70674","text":"Symptom"}]},{"id":"blk-40473","spans":[{"id":"spn-70675","text":"Status"}]}],"id":"blk-40470","kind":"table","rows":